  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "A circular plate of radius $r$ is heated so that the area of the plate is increasing at a rate of 3 cm²/min. At what rate is the radius increasing when $r=5$ cm?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{3}{10\\pi}\\text{ cm/min}$",
      "worked": "$A=\\pi r^2$ and $\\dfrac{dA}{dt}=3\\text{ cm}^2/\\text{min}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dA}{dr}&=2\\pi r\\\\\\frac{dr}{dt}&=\\frac{dr}{dA}\\frac{dA}{dt}\\\\\\frac{dr}{dt}&=\\frac{1}{2\\pi r}(3)\\\\\\frac{dr}{dt}&=\\frac{3}{2\\pi r}\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $r=5$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dr}{dt}&=\\frac{3}{2\\pi(5)}\\\\\\frac{dr}{dt}&=\\frac{3}{10\\pi}\\text{ cm/min}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 34
  },
